bmdmpv for Debian 13 (trixie), amd64
===================================

Install the Blackmagic Desktop Video driver (16.x compatible with SDK 16)
from Blackmagic first. It is an external dependency, not bundled here.

Install the local package with:
    sudo apt install ./bmdmpv_0.1.2-1_amd64.deb

Open bmdmpv from the application menu or run bmdmpv-gui. The command-line
wrapper is mpv-decklink; mpv-decklink --list-modes enumerates HDMI modes.
The system mpv is not replaced. Do not run the GUI as root.

YouTube requires yt-dlp and a supported JavaScript runtime. The app checks
versions and searches PATH, ~/.local/bin, ~/.deno/bin and ~/.bun/bin, so a
desktop launcher can find user-installed runtimes without shell setup.
Deno >= 2.3 is preferred; Node >= 22 is another option. The absolute runtime
path is shared by metadata extraction and playback. See upstream EJS setup:
https://github.com/yt-dlp/yt-dlp/wiki/EJS
Select the logged-in browser under Cookies do YouTube. No cookies, browser
profiles, media files or user settings are included in the package.

Settings remain in ~/.config/bmdmpv (or $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/bmdmpv). Package
removal does not delete personal settings, media or playlists.

This binary targets Debian 13 amd64. Other distributions/releases require
their own builds against their FFmpeg and system-library versions.

Build again from the checkout:
    ./build-probe.sh
    ./build-mpv.sh
    python3 scripts/build-deb.py

Packaging requires dpkg-dev, binutils, patchelf and desktop-file-utils.
PATCHELF can specify a locally extracted patchelf binary. There are no
maintainer scripts, privileged build steps or automatic downloads in the
packaging script. Source build prerequisites are described in README.rst;
the DeckLink SDK stays external. The companion source archive also includes
libplacebo in third_party/libplacebo and the effective Meson build options.
